        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "806dd58c-22d5-5d90-a4a5-9fe2d1ba3597",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Chester Dillon, James C. Klotter\n- Organizations: Georgetown College\n- Roles: Head football coach, History professor, Co-author\n- Places: Homewood, Alabama, Georgetown, Kentucky\n- Topics: College history, Coaching appointments\n\nFacts:\n- Georgetown College was chartered in 1829 and was the first Baptist college west of the Allegheny Mountains.\n- Chester Dillon served as the head football coach at Dakota Wesleyan University from 1915 to 1916.\n- Chester Dillon served as the head football coach at Simpson College from 1916 to 1917.\n- Chester Dillon served as the head football coach at Howard College in Homewood, Alabama, now Samford University, in 1919 and again from 1927 to 1928.\n- Chester Dillon served as the head football coach at Oshkosh State Normal School, now the University of Wisconsin–Oshkosh, in 1920.\n- Chester Dillon served as the head football coach at Georgetown College in Georgetown, Kentucky, from 1929 to 1930.\n- Chester Dillon served as the head football coach at Jacksonville State Teachers College, now Jacksonville State University, from 1938 to 1939 and again in 1945.\n- James C. Klotter is a history professor at Georgetown College.\n- James C. Klotter is one of the co-authors of Kentucky's staple history book \"A New History of Kentucky\".",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "a5eec416-cead-5ea3-b30b-ae81f2861ca7",
        "text": "Page: Chester Dillon. Sentence: He served as the head football coach at Dakota Wesleyan University (1915–1916), Simpson College (1916–1917), Howard College in Homewood, Alabama—now Samford University (1919, 1927–1928), Oshkosh State Normal School—now the University of Wisconsin–Oshkosh (1920), Georgetown College in Georgetown, Kentucky (1929–1930), and Jacksonville State Teachers College—now Jacksonville State University (1938–1939, 1945).\nPage: Georgetown College. Sentence: Chartered in 1829, Georgetown was the first Baptist college west of the Allegheny Mountains.\nPage: James C. Klotter. Sentence: Klotter also is a history professor at Georgetown College and one of the co-authors of Kentucky's staple history book \"A New History of Kentucky\".",
